# eu-1tkk.7.21: an error raised by a prelude combinator that fails
# immediately — no continuation stack, no annotated environment — must
# still blame the user's own call site.
#
# The call site is the only user-file Smid in existence for this error, so
# it survives only if entering the prelude global leaves the caller's
# annotation intact. Stamping a Smid::global_slot identity onto every
# blob-reconstructed prelude global overwrote it, and the diagnostic lost
# its primary label entirely.
#
# The call is made from inside a user-defined helper (line 23) rather than
# at the top-level target (line 21), so the location assertion pins that
# the label tracks the real call site.
#
# The location itself is asserted in
# tests/diagnostics_blame_plumbing_test.rs, gated on prelude_blob_ok: it
# only holds under a blob. In source-prelude mode the annotation is a real
# prelude source position, which to_diagnostic correctly suppresses, so no
# label is emitted and the .expect sidecar here can only assert wording.
` { target: :main requires-io: true }
main: run-it("ignored")

run-it(s): io.shell({ stdin: s })
